Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: flickos-hooks
Architecture: all
# setsid -f (util-linux, essential): the programs that see an event start the
# hooks with it and don't wait for them.
Depends: python3,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: run your own programs when something happens on the FlickOS desktop
 Put an executable file, in any language, in a folder named for an event under
 ~/.config/flickos/hooks/, and FlickOS runs it when the event happens: when the
 screen locks or unlocks, or when the computer wakes up.
 .
 Nothing runs and nothing is added to login while you have no hooks. A hook
 can't hold up the lock screen, runs only as you, and is stopped after thirty
 seconds. The command flickos-hooks lists the events, tests your hooks and
 shows what ran.
